---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { profile } from '../data/profile';
---
<Base title="About" description={`About ${profile.name}: ${profile.roleLine}.`}>
  <article class="stack-lg">
    <header class="stack">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1>{profile.name}</h1>
      <p class="role" style="font-family: var(--font-mono); color: var(--accent)">{profile.title}</p>
    </header>
    <div class="stack prose">
      <p>
        I'm an Enterprise Solution Architect and technical team lead with {profile.experience} years across banking, fintech,
        telecom, Saudi government platforms, education, IoT and enterprise platforms. I started in Java/Jakarta EE, IBM
        WebSphere/FileNet and ISO 8583 banking middleware, and now combine J2EE/JSF modernisation with cloud and network
        architecture, microservices, ESB/API integration, event streaming, cybersecurity and resilience.
      </p>
      <p>
        I define target-state architectures, roadmaps, standards and governance with TOGAF ADM and C4 (L1–L3), and translate
        business needs into scalable solutions. Then I guide cross-functional delivery from discovery and design through
        implementation, integration, release and operations: Kubernetes, Kafka and Debezium CDC, zero-trust networking, GitOps,
        PCI DSS 4.0 controls and applied AI. I treat licences, security boundaries and evidence as first-class design inputs.
      </p>
      <p>
        Today I'm a Principal Solution Architect at Synechron in Riyadh, on the Tahakom engagement, leading enterprise
        architecture across Java, cloud, platform engineering, cybersecurity and AI. Before that I consulted independently on
        IoT platform modernisation, cloud networking, fintech integration and security for the UAE and Iraq markets. I'm also
        building <a href="/work/twinfra">Twinfra</a>, an MIT-licensed, AWS-compatible private cloud, and I write about security
        architecture: see the <a href="/writing/psaf">Product Security Architecture Framework (PSAF)</a>.
      </p>
      <p class="muted">{profile.location}.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
